Z||000000||FIERO1985||12-18-2000||03:14 PM||||Anyone have pace setter tips on their fiero and if so do the dual tip glass packed tips really make much of a diff??<P>Thanks<BR>Dan<P><P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||12-18-2000||03:59 PM||||As opposed to running a muffler?  My dad has Pacesetters on his SC 3.8 (no muffler) and it is very loud and deep. Personally, I don't care for it. I think a Flowmaster sounds much better. <BR>Now, if you mean Pacesetters in addition to the muffler, I have no frame of reference. Sorry.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||12-18-2000||07:48 PM||||Had Pacesetter tips on the 350TPI Countach with a Dynomax muffler. I later removed the glass packing and baffles from the tips just to make them look better. I didn't notice any difference in sound (or performance).<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
